	<!-- ── The problem ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
	<section class="page-section" id="wing-it">
		<div class="tip-row tip-row--flip">
			<div class="tip-row-text">
				<h2>Most crews are winging it</h2>
				<p>Look around the tents at any backyard ultra. Most crews are friends and family who came to help. They care about you more than anyone there. They have also never done this before, so they run on good intentions and no system.</p>
				<p>So things get missed. The food goes on too late. Nobody is sure who is doing what. You end up making the calls yourself between loops, which is the one thing you cannot afford to spend energy on.</p>
				<p>At loop 12 none of that costs you anything. At loop 30 it ends your race.</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="tip-row-img">
				<img src="/assets/img/crew-camp-support.jpeg" alt="A crew member checking in with a runner between loops at a backyard ultra" width="800" height="1067" loading="lazy"/>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ── The system ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
	<section class="page-section" id="systems">
		<div class="tip-row">
			<div class="tip-row-text">
				<h2>What changes when we are in your tent</h2>
				<p>We do not write your race plan. You have one. We study it, we go through your preferences with you, and we share our experience where it helps.</p>
				<p>Then during the race our systems keep things tight and crisp, so all you have to worry about is running. That means:</p>
				<ul class="learn-list">
					<li>Your fueling is on point.</li>
					<li>You get the maximum amount of rest each loop.</li>
					<li>Your tent stays organized.</li>
					<li>You are not making decisions on behalf of your crew.</li>
					<li>Everyone in the tent has a clear role.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<figure class="tip-row-img">
				<img src="/assets/img/byu-tips-race-box.jpeg" alt="An organized race box in a backyard ultra crew tent" width="600" height="750" loading="lazy"/>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

